#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# random_real

#% text
# `random_real()` gives a uniformly distributed machine real in [0, 1).

#% text
# `random_real(b)` gives a uniform real in [0, b).

#% text
# `random_real([a, b])` gives a uniform real in [a, b).

#% text
# `random_real(range, n)` gives a list of `n` such reals; `random_real(range, [n1, n2, ...])` gives nested lists.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The numbers come from the session's generator; `seed(k)` makes them repeatable.

#% item
# The ends may be any real numbers, exact or inexact, or closed numeric expressions such as `pi`; `a` must not exceed `b`.

#% item
# A list of numbers drawn at once is the same as the same number of single draws.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A number between 0 and 1:

#% cell
seed(1); random_real()
#% output
#= 0.4219463724596497

#% text
# Between 0 and 10:

#% cell
random_real(10)
#% output
#= 6.413152138724026

#% text
# Between -1 and 1:

#% cell
random_real([-1, 1])
#% output
#= -0.44204816920710077

#% text
# Four numbers:

#% cell
random_real([0, 1], 4)
#% output
#= [0.04373894403144052, 0.8968298384314126, 0.07900383719904425, 0.20179147560471555]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A 2 x 3 array:

#% cell
random_real(1, [2, 3])
#% output
#= [[0.38170935472141676, 0.7747576805661607, 0.275631237785959], [0.9213178355622352, 0.5757369651451368, 0.979494810489959]]

#% text
# An end given as a closed expression:

#% cell
random_real([pi, 4])
#% output
#= 3.9391755715400643

#% text
# An empty list:

#% cell
random_real([0, 1], 0)
#% output
#= []

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Estimate pi from the fraction of random points of the square [0, 1] x [0, 1] that lie inside the quarter circle:

#% cell
seed(3); pts = random_real(1, [20000, 2]); 4*count_if(pts, p => p[1]^2 + p[2]^2 < 1)/20000.0
#% output
#= 3.1204

#% text
# A Monte Carlo estimate of the integral of exp(-x^2) over [0, 1], and the exact value:

#% cell
seed(4); mean(map(x => exp(-x^2), random_real([0, 1], 20000)))
#% output
#= 0.746192616600769

#% cell
n_integrate(exp(-x^2), [x, 0, 1])
#% output
#= 0.7468241328124272

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The mean of many uniform numbers is close to 1/2, and their variance close to 1/12:

#% cell
seed(5); u = random_real([0, 1], 10^4); [mean(u), variance(u), 1/12.0]
#% output
#= [0.5013935124190826, 0.08379382942363774, 0.08333333333333333]

#% text
# The same draws as `random_variate` of the uniform distribution:

#% cell
seed(6); random_real([0, 1], 2)
#% output
#= [0.7426042934169479, 0.3657268086662666]

#% cell
seed(6); random_variate(uniform_distribution([0, 1]), 2)
#% output
#= [0.7426042934169479, 0.3657268086662666]

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# The lower end must not exceed the upper one:

#% cell
random_real([5, 2])
#% output
#! failure(argument, random_real, "the range must be a real b >= 0 or a list [a, b] of reals with a <= b")

#% text
# A symbolic range is not allowed:

#% cell
random_real(b)
#% output
#! failure(argument, random_real, "the range must be a real b >= 0 or a list [a, b] of reals with a <= b")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `seed`, `random_integer`, `random_normal`, `random_variate`, `uniform_distribution`, `random_choice`
